# A shell script with CRLF line endings cannot run: the interpreter sees `\r` as
# part of the command. `scripts/check.sh` is executed by CI on all three OSes.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The four completion scripts and the man page are generated with `\n` and
# compared byte for byte by `scripts/check.sh completions`, on three operating
# systems: a checkout that rewrote them to CRLF would fail that gate for a reason
# that has nothing to do with the binary. `-text` keeps the bytes exactly as
# `crates/lrsalvage-cli/examples/artifacts.rs` writes them.
crates/lrsalvage-cli/artifacts/** -text
